"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Net cash of $335.8m against total assets of $821.4m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.1% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"}],"bear":[{"text":"Insiders disposed of 83.2% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (440,825 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526263764/0001193125-26-263764-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.1% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526263764/0001193125-26-263764-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 45.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.45,"consecutive":2,"current":0.527,"current_display":"52.7%","threshold_display":"45.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"